<hr>
<h3><a name="OVERVIEW">OVERVIEW</a></h3>
<p>NACSCORP, a wholly-owned subsidiary of the National Association of College Stores, was established to provide 
products and services for NACS member stores. Our mission is to build long-term relationships with our customers by 
helping each one of them succeed. All of our customers are college bookstores or other educational resellers. </p>
<p>NACSCORP distributes products which are of particular importance to the students, faculty, and staff of college and 
university campuses. We currently list over 60,000 titles from more than 500 publishers and manufacturers. In general, 
we provide content products, such as books and multimedia titles; and tools important in education, such as computer 
hardware and software. </p>
<p>Our book selection consists of a wide variety of adult paperback and hardback; mass market titles; university press and 
other academic titles; reference books; test preparation and study guides; professional and technical titles; computer 
books; children's books; and an assortment of remainders. </p>
<p>Our growing selection of computer hardware, peripherals, and supplies includes CPUs, monitors, laptops, CD-ROM 
drives, and modems. We have a large selection of software, with educational pricing (significant discounts for faculty and 
students) on many titles. NACSCORP also carries the latest multimedia, edutainment, and reference titles on CD. </p>
<p>Our services and policies were created in direct response to the needs of our customers. Below is an outline of our 
services; our policies on shipping, payments, and returns; and a listing of NACSCORP staff contacts. <b><i>If you have any 
comments or suggestions, please let us know. We are here to help!</i></b></p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
<h3><a name="Ordering">ORDERING </a></h3>
<p><b><i>For order placement, pricing, availability, and questions concerning your orders:</i></b> </p>
<p><b>Phone</b>: 800/ 321-3883 or 216/ 775-7777 ext. 2573 (US and Canada)<br>
<i>Order hours (Eastern Time): 8 AM-7 PM Monday-Thursday; 8 AM-6 PM Friday <br>
</i><b>Fax</b>: 800/ 344-5059 or 216/ 774-1335 (US Only) <br>
<b>PUBNET SAN</b>: 134-2118 <br>
<b>Easylink</b> (Telex): 62-820233<br>
<b>Internet Address: </b>62820233@eln.attmail.com <br>
<b>WWW Access</b> (product availability only): http://www.nacscorp.com/ </p>
<p>All phone orders are confirmed for availability immediately on the phone. We pick up other types of orders several times 
a day to assure timely confirmation of your purchase order requests. </p>
<p>When you call to place an order, please have the following information ready: </p>
<ul>
<li>Your account number (NACS store number) </li>
<li>PO number </li>
<li>Shipping instructions </li>
<li>Part numbers (ISBN or UPC) </li>
<li>Author, title, and publisher (for book orders), <b>OR</b> product name, platform, manufacturer (for computer product 
orders) </li>
<li>Quantity </li>
</ul>
<p><b>Backorders</b> </p>
<p>To backorder titles, simply specify on your order, or to one of our phone representatives, that you would like to 
backorder. Please include backorder shipping instructions. We will then automatically reserve and commit stock to your 
order as it arrives. </p>
<p><b>Future Orders / Bin &amp; Holds</b> </p>
<p>NACSCORP's Bin &amp; Hold program allows you to use our warehouse to hold your stock until you're ready to receive it. 
Especially important for back-to-class time, the Bin &amp; Hold program allows you to start your orders early, then add or 
subtract quantities or titles as needed.</p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
<h3><a name="Shipping">SHIPPING </a></h3>
<p>Orders are shipped within 48 hours (excluding weekends and holidays) from the time they are placed. We can provide 
same-day shipping on &quot;RUSH&quot; orders placed before 1:30 p.m..</p>
<p>Your account can be set up to accommodate your store's ordering, shipping, and invoicing needs. We can set up your 
account so that you can place orders, receive backorders, and be invoiced for all products under one account number. 
Or, if you prefer, we can set up separate entity accounts for textbooks, general books, and computer products. Please 
specify your preferences to one of our Order Entry Representatives. </p>
<p>All shipments are sent FOB, Oberlin, Ohio. Shipments via NACSCORP selected carriers can be prepaid by 
NACSCORP and added to your invoice. </p>
<p><b>Special Orders</b> <br>
<br>
In addition to our regularly stocked items, NACSCORP lists approximately 20,000 different titles which we can special 
order for you. Please allow three to five weeks for delivery of special order items. </p>
<p>Drop shipping and direct shipping are available in some cases. (Drop shipping is not available for computer products.) </p>
<p><b>Savings on Shipping Costs</b> <br>
<br>
The <i>NACSCORP 2-Day Freight Program</i> can save you money and allow you to receive orders faster. We offer 
guaranteed two-day air delivery at roughly 50% off standard rates of other popular carriers. For stores in the west, this 
equates to two-day air service at Zone 8 ground rates. </p>
<p>The <i>NACS Freight Program</i> offers shipping discounts of 57% or more on truck orders. To learn more about this 
program, call the NACS Transportation Services Department at NACS (800/622-7498 ext. 2307). </p>
<p><b>Damaged merchandise and mis-shipments <br>
<br>
</b>If you receive damaged or defective merchandise or a mis-shipment, please notify us immediately by calling our 
Customer Service Line (800/458-9303). </p>
<p>Notification of damaged or defective merchandise must be made within 30 days of receipt. If the product is damaged 
during shipment, please notify the carrier immediately and retain the damaged box for inspection by the carrier.</p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
<h3><a name="PAYMENT">PAYMENT TERMS </a></h3>
<p>Net 30-day terms. Delayed billing (extended terms) is available in fall and spring to qualified accounts. </p>
<p>Items on your invoice can be arranged alphabetically by title, author, or publisher; or they can be listed in the same way 
that you place the order. </p>
<p><b>Credit Swap <br>
<br>
</b>Our <i>Credit Swap</i> program allows you to exchange your unused publisher credit memos for either 80% of the amount as 
a NACSCORP credit or 70% as cash. This offer is good for credit memos from a select list of publishers. Please call 
our Finance Department (800/622-7498 ext. 2236) for more information. </p>
<p><b>Discount Policy</b> <br>
<br>
<b><i>No minimum order quantity! <br>
</i></b>Books are discounted 40% on most titles. Many short discount and net-priced titles are available; all computer products 
are net priced. Call our Inbound Sales Department for the most recent catalogs, price lists, and special promotional 
offers. Further discounts are available to large volume accounts. Call our Special Programs Department for details 
(800/334-9882 ext. 2585).</p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
<h3><a name="RETURNS">RETURNS </a></h3>
<p><b>No returns penalties! <br>
</b>For most products we will grant a full return credit as long as the items are in saleable condition (including the absence of 
store price stickers) and are returned within 18 months of the invoice date. </p>
<p>A small percentage of our products will have shorter return periods for one of the following reasons: 1) the release of a 
new version of a product has made the old version obsolete, 2) a title has gone out of print or a product discontinued, or 
3) there are special vendor stipulations which cause NACSCORP to have a shorter return period. </p>
<p>When any of these situations arise for products you have purchased within the last 18 months, you will be notified of 
return deadlines via our <i>NACSCORP Book Returns Notice </i>or our<i> Computer Products Returns Notice,</i> which will 
automatically be sent to you along with <b>Expedited Return</b> shipping labels. When you use the <b>Expedited Return</b> labels, 
please include only items that are listed in your returns notice. (Include other items in a separate shipment.) </p>
<p><b>Address For Returns:</b> </p>
<address>Returns Department </address>
<address>NACSCORP </address>
<address>528 East Lorain St. </address>
<address>Oberlin, Ohio 44074-1298 </address>
<p>In order for NACSCORP to properly credit your account in a timely manner, returns should be prepared according to 
the following guidelines: </p>
<p><b>Guidelines For Preparing Returns:</b> </p>
<ul>
<li>If your store is equipped to prepare a computer-generated list of items you are returning, we encourage you to do 
that. For <b>each item</b>, be sure to include: </li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><b>Part number</b> (ISBN or UPC) <br>
<b>Invoice number </b>from the original purchase <br>
<b>Price</b> <b>information</b> <br>
<b>OR</b> <br>
If you cannot readily generate your own list, please provide the necessary information by <b>photocopying 
the NACSCORP invoice</b> form. Highlight the items you are returning and indicate the <b>quantity</b> you are 
sending back. </p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>Put the packing list in a window envelope on the outside of one of the boxes <b>OR</b> mark <b>&quot;Packing List 
Enclosed&quot;</b> on the box that contains the list. </li>
<li><b>Number all of your boxes</b> so we know they are all part of the same shipment (e.g. 1 of 3, 2 of 3, 3 of 3). We 
encourage you to reuse boxes to cut down on waste but please be sure to cross out any old references to box 
numbers or shipping information. </li>
<li>Mark your store's <b>Charge Back Number</b> and at least one <b>Invoice Number</b> on <b>all boxes</b> so that they will be 
linked together and linked to your store's account. </li>
<li>In certain cases our Customer Service Reps give out RMAs. If you have been given an RMA for a return, please 
use the <b>Expedited Return</b> labels and record your RMA in the space provided. </li>
</ul>
<p>Using our<b> Expedited Return</b> shipping labels (when returning products listed in the returns notices or for returns that 
require an RMA) and our <b>General Return</b> shipping labels (for any other returns) will help your staff prepare returns 
according to the guidelines and help us process them more efficiently. <b>General Return</b> labels can be ordered from 
NACSCORP.</p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
<h3><a name="CATALOGS">CATALOGS AND MERCHANDISING AIDS<b> </b></a></h3>
<p><b>Catalog Information</b> <br>
<br>
NACSCORP publishes the following catalogs: <i>Inventory Catalog</i> (April), a complete listing of all titles; <i>Computer 
Products Catalog</i>, store version (August, December, April); <i>Campus Computing Sourcebook</i>, consumer version 
(August, January); <i>Dictionary and Reference Catalog</i> (May); <i>Study Guides and Test Preparation Catalog</i> (August); 
<i>Calendar Catalog</i>; <i>Computer Books Catalog</i>; <i>Remainders Catalog</i>. </p>
<p>Call our Inbound Sales department at 800/321-3883 for a free catalog. Catalog information is also available on 
microfiche, diskette and the World Wide Web. </p>
<p><b>Calendar of Book Promotions</b> <br>
<br>
NACSCORP produces a calendar of promotions centered around events that are important on the college campus. 
Examples of these promotions are Nature &amp; Ecology (Earth Day), African American History Month, Children's Book 
Week, Women's History Month, and Banned Book Week. NACSCORP selects titles for each theme, and provides 
effective merchandising and advertising materials to maximize your sales. Please contact our Special Programs 
Department (800/622-7498 ext. 2355) for a complete listing of these promotions. </p>
<p><b>Automatic Shipment Programs</b> <br>
<br>
NACSCORP provides a number of Automatic Shipment Programs that make it much easier for your store to buy and 
manage inventory. New title information, plan-o-grams, and inventory monitoring sheets are included, as well as return 
packing lists sent to you when titles go off the program. You can choose from the following programs: New Releases, 
New York Times Bestsellers, Computer Books, Reference Books, Educational Resource Books, Business Books, and 
Children's Books. Please call our Special Programs Department at (800/622-7498 ext. 2355) for more details. </p>
<p><b>Recommended Stock List <br>
<br>
</b>The NACSCORP Merchandising Staff compiles a list of recommended books for various subject areas. The complete 
list is included in the back of our Inventory Catalog, and updates are mailed out every month. </p>
<p><b>Computer Products</b> <br>
<br>
Our Merchandising Department provides information and merchandising materials that allow you to confidently retail 
computer products. We work with our suppliers to design materials specifically for college stores. Catalogs, flyers, 
point-of-purchase signs, and other items are available. You can sign up for a year's worth of materials with one 
convenient order form, and automatically receive items as they become available. This program is available to 
NACSCORP customers at no charge! </p>
<p>Pre-packs of best selling titles are available as the <i>Bestseller Kit </i>and<i> Mini Bestseller Kit</i>; these kits can also be tailored 
to meet the specific needs of your store. </p>
<p>If you would like to start carrying computer products in your store, ask any of our Order Entry Representatives to send 
you a reseller authorization form. When you become an authorized reseller, you can buy computer products at 
educational discounts (for products with educational pricing). You will also receive our confidential price list every month 
and our weekly <i>Ear to the Ground</i> fax newsletter, which will keep you up-to-date on new computer product releases, 
price changes, and industry information. </p>
<p><b>Display</b> <b>and Promotional Materials</b> </p>
<p>A variety of &quot;turn-key&quot; merchandising and marketing materials are available to facilitate the growth of your store's book 
and computer product departments. Let NACSCORP serve as your own advertising and printing departments! (Items 
which we design for the end-user are printed with &quot;from the college store&quot; on them.) Professionally designed and printed 
flyers, signage, shelf-talkers, display kits, and catalogs are available.</p>
<p><a href="#TOC"><font size=2>Return to Table of Contents</font></a></p>
